      "Working and herding breeds — Border Collies, Australian Shepherds, Belgian Malinois, Huskies, Vizslas, German Shorthaired Pointers — were selectively bred over centuries for eight-hour days of physically demanding, mentally engaged labour. Ninety minutes of structured exercise plus deliberate cognitive work is the floor, not the ceiling. Under-exercised working dogs do not become lazy; they become destructive, vocal, and frequently misdiagnosed as 'anxious' when the actual problem is unmet biological need. If your lifestyle cannot reliably provide this, these are not the right breeds for you — a hard truth worth saying out loud.",
